- name: epy_block_0
  id: epy_block
  parameters:
    _source_code: "\nimport numpy as np\nfrom gnuradio import gr\n\n\nclass blk(gr.sync_block):\n\
      \    \"\"\"Frame-sync assistance for the carrier loops (the software version\
      \ of what the FPGA does). Sits between the polyphase clock sync (1 sample per\
      \ symbol) and the Costas loop.\n    d_n = m_n conj(m_(n-1)) is the phase step\
      \ between symbols: 2 pi f T for the m-sequence preamble steps (0 or 180 degrees,\
      \ the chips of x^6 + x + 1) plus the frequency offset. The 63 chips are\n  \
      \  correlated with the unit-length steps: at the end of the preamble |C|/63\
      \ is large and arg(C) = 2 pi f T, the carrier offset per symbol, without any\
      \ loop and whatever the carrier phase\n    (+- 480 kHz at 960 ksym/s). From\
      \ the symbol after the peak on, the stream is rotated by exp(-j phase) with\
      \ that frequency (an NCO), so the Costas loop behind starts on frequency.\n\
      \    Parameters: thr = detection threshold on |C|/63 (noise alone: 0.13 rms,\
      \ a clean preamble: 1), assist = 1 applies the rotation, 0 passes the stream\
      \ through (the estimate is still made),\n    smooth = weight of a new estimate\
      \ (1 = take it as it is), sym_rate for the output in Hz. Outputs: 0 the symbols,\
      \ 1 the frequency estimate in Hz, 2 the number of preambles found.\"\"\"\n\n\
      \    def __init__(self, thr=0.5, assist=1, smooth=0.5, sym_rate=960000.0):\n\
      \        gr.sync_block.__init__(self, name=\"Preamble frequency assist\", in_sig=[np.complex64],\
      \ out_sig=[np.complex64, np.float32, np.float32])\n        self.thr = float(thr);\
      \ self.assist = int(assist); self.smooth = float(smooth); self.sym_rate = float(sym_rate)\n\
      \        a = [1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]\n        while len(a) < 63:\n            n =\
      \ len(a) - 6\n            a.append(a[n + 1] ^ a[n])\n        chips = 1.0 - 2.0\
      \ * np.array(a, dtype=np.float64)           # bit 0 = step 0 (chip +1), bit\
      \ 1 = step 180 degrees (chip -1)\n        self.h = chips[::-1].astype(np.complex128)\n\
      \        self.last_m = 1.0 + 0j; self.dtail = np.zeros(62, dtype=np.complex128)\n\
      \        self.mprev = 0.0; self.cprev = 0j; self.since = 10 ** 9\n        self.w_est\
      \ = 0.0; self.have = False; self.phase = 0.0; self.hits = 0\n\n    def work(self,\
      \ input_items, output_items):\n        x = input_items[0].astype(np.complex128);\
      \ n = len(x)\n        prev = np.concatenate([[self.last_m], x[:-1]]); d = x\
      \ * np.conj(prev)\n        mag = np.abs(d); du = np.where(mag > 1e-9, d / np.maximum(mag,\
      \ 1e-9), 1.0)\n        self.last_m = x[-1]\n        ext = np.concatenate([self.dtail,\
      \ du]); self.dtail = ext[-62:]\n        corr = np.convolve(ext, self.h, mode=\"\
      valid\") if len(ext) >= 63 else np.zeros(n, dtype=np.complex128)\n        cm\
      \ = np.abs(corr) / 63.0\n        M = np.concatenate([[self.mprev], cm]); C =\
      \ np.concatenate([[self.cprev], corr])\n        self.mprev = cm[-1]; self.cprev\
      \ = corr[-1]\n        w_arr = None; w_cur = self.w_est if self.assist else 0.0\n\
      \        trig = []\n        if len(M) > 2:\n            j = np.nonzero((M[1:-1]\
      \ >= self.thr) & (M[1:-1] >= M[:-2]) & (M[1:-1] > M[2:]))[0] + 1   # local maxima\
      \ (one-symbol look-ahead); M[j] is chunk index j - 1\n            last = -(10\
      \ ** 9)\n            for jj in j:\n                if jj - last < 32 and last\
      \ > -(10 ** 9): continue\n                last = jj; trig.append(jj - 1)\n \
      \               est = float(np.angle(C[jj]))\n                self.w_est = est\
      \ if not self.have else self.w_est + self.smooth * (est - self.w_est)\n    \
      \            self.have = True; self.hits += 1\n        if self.assist:\n   \
      \         w_arr = np.full(n, w_cur)\n            for t in trig:\n          \
      \      w_arr[min(max(t + 1, 0), n):] = self.w_est\n            ph = self.phase\
      \ + np.cumsum(w_arr)\n            self.phase = float(np.mod(ph[-1], 2 * np.pi))\n\
      \            out = x * np.exp(-1j * ph)\n        else:\n            self.phase\
      \ = 0.0; out = x\n        output_items[0][:] = out.astype(np.complex64)\n  \
      \      output_items[1][:] = np.float32(self.w_est / (2 * np.pi) * self.sym_rate)\n\
      \        output_items[2][:] = np.float32(self.hits)\n        return n\n"
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    assist: assist_on
    comment: ''
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
    smooth: '0.5'
    sym_rate: samp_rate/sps
    thr: '0.5'
  states:
    _io_cache: '(''Preamble frequency assist'', ''blk'', [(''thr'', ''0.5''), (''assist'',
      ''1''), (''smooth'', ''0.5''), (''sym_rate'', ''960000.0'')], [(''0'', ''complex'',
      1)], [(''0'', ''complex'', 1), (''1'', ''float'', 1), (''2'', ''float'', 1)],
      ''Frame-sync assistance for the carrier loops (the software version of what
      the FPGA does). Sits between the polyphase clock sync (1 sample per symbol)
      and the Costas loop.\n    d_n = m_n conj(m_(n-1)) is the phase step between
      symbols: 2 pi f T for the m-sequence preamble steps (0 or 180 degrees, the chips
      of x^6 + x + 1) plus the frequency offset. The 63 chips are\n    correlated
      with the unit-length steps: at the end of the preamble |C|/63 is large and arg(C)
      = 2 pi f T, the carrier offset per symbol, without any loop and whatever the
      carrier phase\n    (+- 480 kHz at 960 ksym/s). From the symbol after the peak
      on, the stream is rotated by exp(-j phase) with that frequency (an NCO), so
      the Costas loop behind starts on frequency.\n    Parameters: thr = detection
      threshold on |C|/63 (noise alone: 0.13 rms, a clean preamble: 1), assist = 1
      applies the rotation, 0 passes the stream through (the estimate is still made),\n    smooth
      = weight of a new estimate (1 = take it as it is), sym_rate for the output in
      Hz. Outputs: 0 the symbols, 1 the frequency estimate in Hz, 2 the number of
      preambles found.'', [''assist'', ''smooth'', ''sym_rate'', ''thr''])'
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [1480, 120]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: epy_block_1
  id: epy_block
  parameters:
    _source_code: "\nimport numpy as np\nfrom gnuradio import gr\n\n\nclass blk(gr.sync_block):\n\
      \    \"\"\"Frame synchroniser and bit error counter of the frame receiver. Input:\
      \ the decoded bits, one per byte, two per symbol (after the differential decoder\
      \ and the symbol map: the bits that were sent).\n    A frame is 64 preamble\
      \ symbols (128 bits: symbol 0 = 00, then 00 for a chip +1 and 11 for a chip\
      \ -1 of the m-sequence x^6 + x + 1) followed by payload_syms symbols of PRBS-15\
      \ restarted in every frame.\n    The preamble is found by the Hamming distance\
      \ of 128 bits to the known pattern (<= dmax; random data are at 64 +- 6, so\
      \ a false match is practically impossible); then the 2 x payload_syms bits\n\
      \    that follow are compared with the PRBS-15 (a known pattern: every error\
      \ counts once).\n    Output 0: the bit error rate over about the last window_frames\
      \ frames (0.5 until a frame is found). Output 1: the frames found since the\
      \ start.\n    Output 2: 1 while the last frame was found one frame period after\
      \ the one before (locked).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, payload_syms=960,\
      \ dmax=16, window_frames=2000):\n        gr.sync_block.__init__(self, name=\"\
      Frame sync + BER\", in_sig=[np.uint8], out_sig=[np.float32, np.float32, np.float32])\n\
      \        self.pl = int(payload_syms); self.dmax = int(dmax); self.win = float(window_frames)\n\
      \        a = [1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]\n        while len(a) < 63:\n            n =\
      \ len(a) - 6\n            a.append(a[n + 1] ^ a[n])\n        pre = [0, 0]\n\
      \        for b in a:\n            pre += [1, 1] if b else [0, 0]\n        self.pre\
      \ = np.array(pre, dtype=np.uint8)\n        s, pay = 0x7FFF, []\n        for\
      \ i in range(2 * self.pl):\n            pay.append((s >> 14) & 1)\n        \
      \    s = ((s << 1) & 0x7FFF) | (((s >> 14) ^ (s >> 13)) & 1)\n        self.pay\
      \ = np.array(pay, dtype=np.uint8)\n        self.fb = 2 * (64 + self.pl)    \
      \                   # frame length in bits\n        self.need = 128 + 2 * self.pl\
      \                      # a whole frame (preamble + payload) must be in the buffer\n\
      \        self.buf = np.zeros(0, dtype=np.uint8); self.base = 0       # absolute\
      \ bit index of buf[0]\n        self.next_scan = 0                          \
      \       # absolute index: nothing before it is searched\n        self.frames\
      \ = 0; self.m = 0.0; self.n = 0.0; self.ber = 0.5; self.locked_flag = 0.0; self.last_q\
      \ = None\n\n    def work(self, input_items, output_items):\n        x = input_items[0]\n\
      \        self.buf = np.concatenate([self.buf, x & 1])\n        start = max(self.next_scan\
      \ - self.base, 0)\n        while len(self.buf) - start >= self.need:\n     \
      \       last = len(self.buf) - self.need               # last position whose\
      \ whole frame is present\n            win = np.lib.stride_tricks.sliding_window_view(self.buf[start:last\
      \ + 128], 128)\n            dist = np.count_nonzero(win != self.pre, axis=1)\n\
      \            hit = np.nonzero(dist <= self.dmax)[0]\n            if len(hit)\
      \ == 0:\n                start = last + 1                           # nothing\
      \ in this stretch; the rest arrives with the next bits\n                break\n\
      \            k = int(hit[0]); k += int(np.argmin(dist[k:k + 4]))\n         \
      \   q = start + k\n            err = float(np.count_nonzero(self.buf[q + 128:q\
      \ + self.need] != self.pay))\n            kk = np.exp(-1.0 / self.win)\n   \
      \         self.m = self.m * kk + err; self.n = self.n * kk + 2 * self.pl\n \
      \           self.ber = self.m / self.n\n            self.frames += 1\n     \
      \       absq = self.base + q\n            self.locked_flag = 1.0 if (self.last_q\
      \ is not None and abs(absq - self.last_q - self.fb) <= 4) else 0.0\n       \
      \     self.last_q = absq\n            self.next_scan = absq + self.fb - 16 \
      \          # the next preamble is one frame later (a margin for a lost or added\
      \ bit)\n            start = max(self.next_scan - self.base, 0)\n        self.next_scan\
      \ = self.base + start\n        cut = min(start, len(self.buf))\n        if cut\
      \ > 0:\n            self.buf = self.buf[cut:]; self.base += cut\n        output_items[0][:]\
      \ = self.ber; output_items[1][:] = self.frames; output_items[2][:] = self.locked_flag\n\
      \        return len(x)\n"
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: ''
    dmax: '16'
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
    payload_syms: payload_syms
    window_frames: '2000'
  states:
    _io_cache: '(''Frame sync + BER'', ''blk'', [(''payload_syms'', ''960''), (''dmax'',
      ''16''), (''window_frames'', ''2000'')], [(''0'', ''byte'', 1)], [(''0'', ''float'',
      1), (''1'', ''float'', 1), (''2'', ''float'', 1)], ''Frame synchroniser and
      bit error counter of the frame receiver. Input: the decoded bits, one per byte,
      two per symbol (after the differential decoder and the symbol map: the bits
      that were sent).\n    A frame is 64 preamble symbols (128 bits: symbol 0 = 00,
      then 00 for a chip +1 and 11 for a chip -1 of the m-sequence x^6 + x + 1) followed
      by payload_syms symbols of PRBS-15 restarted in every frame.\n    The preamble
      is found by the Hamming distance of 128 bits to the known pattern (<= dmax;
      random data are at 64 +- 6, so a false match is practically impossible); then
      the 2 x payload_syms bits\n    that follow are compared with the PRBS-15 (a
      known pattern: every error counts once).\n    Output 0: the bit error rate over
      about the last window_frames frames (0.5 until a frame is found). Output 1:
      the frames found since the start.\n    Output 2: 1 while the last frame was
      found one frame period after the one before (locked).'', [''dmax''])'
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [1060, 420]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
